  {:name :process-sequence-remove
   :description "DELETE /api/sequence/item/:item-id — remove one binding-list-item. The two validation guards and the success path are a flat `:cond` — `[invalid-id? → 400, not-found? → 404, true → apply]`. `:cond` is lazy, so the DB delete runs only when both guards pass. `parsed` + `item` are shared sub-results bound once at the `:cond` fn-def."
   :parent :cond
   :args {:clauses [:_seq-remove-item-id-invalid?  :_seq-remove-err-invalid-item-id
